---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — QuiltClarity"
  description="How QuiltClarity handles saved projects, site analytics, email, and future advertising."
  pageType="article"
>
  <article class="page article-page">
    <header class="hero compact-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>How QuiltClarity handles your information</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Your quilting calculations run in your browser. This page explains what
        stays on your device, what the site measures, and what happens when you
        choose to share a result or email us.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="article-body">
      <section>
        <h2>Projects and browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          QuiltClarity has no account or cloud project store. The planner saves
          your project in this browser's local storage so you can return to it.
          Project names, fabric details, cut lists, measurements, and results
          are not sent to QuiltClarity's analytics service. You can remove saved
          site data through your browser's settings; doing so also removes your
          saved project and preferences on that browser.
        </p>
        <p>
          Local storage also holds your light or dark theme choice and a
          date-only marker used to determine whether a tool visit is a return
          visit. The marker is not a visitor identifier. QuiltClarity does not
          set a cookie for these features.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Sharing, copying, and downloads</h2>
        <p>
          Copy summary puts the displayed summary on your clipboard. Share
          result opens your device's share sheet with the summary and your
          project name, if you entered one. The service or person you select to
          share with then handles that content under their own terms. Printing
          and PDF export are prepared in your browser. You choose where a PDF is
          saved or sent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Site analytics and hosting</h2>
        <p>
          On the public site, QuiltClarity sends a page visit and limited tool
          actions to a same-origin analytics endpoint. The stored record
          contains the page's canonical path and fixed action categories, such
          as which tool was opened. Some tool events include fixed categories or
          count ranges and a boolean return-visit category. The analytics record
          does not contain project content, URL queries or fragments, cookies,
          visitor IDs, IP addresses, browser headers, or referrers. Analytics
          Engine retains these records for three months.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a>{
            ' '
          }
          hosts the site and handles ordinary network request metadata to deliver
          pages and the analytics endpoint. The browser sends no QuiltClarity analytics
          when Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control is enabled. Analytics failures
          do not stop the tools. You can also clear the return-visit marker through
          your browser's site-data settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          QuiltClarity has requested Google AdSense review. The site currently
          has an account-verification tag, but does not load advertising scripts
          or serve ads. No advertising cookies or ad requests are initiated by
          QuiltClarity at this stage.
        </p>
        <p>
          If advertising is enabled later, this page will describe the actual
          setup before ads are served. Google's advertising services and its
          partners may use cookies to show ads based on visits to this and other
          sites. You can learn about Google's advertising data practices and
          choices at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads"
            >Google's advertising privacy page</a
          > and manage personalized ads at <a
            href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">My Ad Center</a
          >. Any required consent controls must be in place before ad serving.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions or corrections, email{' '}
          <a href="mailto:contact@quiltclarity.com">contact@quiltclarity.com</a
          >. Cloudflare Email Routing forwards messages to our Gmail inbox, so
          those providers handle the message to deliver it. See{' '}
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
            >Google's privacy policy</a
          >{' '}
          for Gmail's practices. Please avoid including sensitive project information
          unless it is needed for your request.
        </p>
      </section>
      <p>Last updated: 8 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
